1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:03,924
The hardest moment on shift is not always clinical.

2
00:00:03,924 --> 00:00:06,619
Sometimes, it is the next sentence you say.

3
00:00:06,619 --> 00:00:08,089
To a frightened family.

4
00:00:08,089 --> 00:00:09,191
To a busy doctor.

5
00:00:09,191 --> 00:00:11,580
To the colleague taking over from you.

6
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:14,904
What do I say?

7
00:00:14,904 --> 00:00:17,680
How do I escalate without sounding unsure?

8
00:00:17,680 --> 00:00:19,940
Did my handover really make sense?

9
00:00:20,540 --> 00:00:21,163
Breathe.

10
00:00:21,163 --> 00:00:24,821
These are skills, and skills can be practised.

11
00:00:24,821 --> 00:00:26,300
Carecraft has you.

12
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:31,601
Every day, one moment from a working shift.

13
00:00:31,601 --> 00:00:34,141
Think first, then compare your reasoning.

14
00:00:34,141 --> 00:00:38,980
The feedback names the behaviour, and gives you one specific thing to try next.

15
00:00:50,283 --> 00:00:54,712
Thirty short lessons for the work you do, from foundation to advanced.

16
00:00:54,712 --> 00:00:59,078
Read, practise and reflect, with your own notes beside every lesson.

17
00:00:59,078 --> 00:01:01,103
Or learn as a guided slideshow.

18
00:01:12,367 --> 00:01:16,324
Ninety illustrated guides you can zoom, save and share.

19
00:01:16,324 --> 00:01:17,978
Listen with intention.

20
00:01:17,978 --> 00:01:19,561
Explain with clarity.

21
00:01:19,561 --> 00:01:21,647
Make numbers mean something.

22
00:01:34,450 --> 00:01:37,582
An animated handover shows the message in order.

23
00:01:37,582 --> 00:01:42,084
Spot the hand hygiene moment in a ward scene, with no time pressure.

24
00:01:42,084 --> 00:01:43,650
Watch, decide, reflect.

25
00:01:56,533 --> 00:02:01,068
Build a clear handover step by step, with worked examples beside you.

26
00:02:01,068 --> 00:02:04,421
Situation, background, assessment, recommendation.

27
00:02:04,421 --> 00:02:07,773
Fictional practice drafts, never clinical records.

28
00:02:18,617 --> 00:02:23,817
See the skills you have rehearsed, from communicating to escalating to wellbeing.

29
00:02:23,817 --> 00:02:26,577
It shows coverage, not a competence score.

30
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:41,570
Thirty lessons.

31
00:02:41,570 --> 00:02:42,992
Ninety visual guides.

32
00:02:42,992 --> 00:02:45,060
Twenty two practice activities.

33
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:52,105
Carecraft is free to start.

34
00:02:52,105 --> 00:02:56,021
The full app comes with the Crown Pass, with seven days free.

35
00:02:56,021 --> 00:02:57,600
One useful minute a day.
